    "note": "Enrolled 2018-08-16 (Senate vote). Assembly voted 2018-05-03 on the Introduced text (2018-02-14); its gun parts are identical in effect to the enrolled text (the introduced version's marked-up changes to Sections 18140 and 18145 yield the same wording). Struck by the bill: 'order is obtained orally,' (18140(a)); the written-petition requirement and the oral-search-warrant procedure under Section 1526 (18145)."
  },
  "operative_text": "Section 18140 (Penal Code): (a) If the request is made orally, sign a declaration under penalty of perjury reciting the oral statements provided to the judicial officer and memorialize the order of the court on the form approved by the Judicial Council.\nSection 18145 (Penal Code): (a) (1) A judicial officer may issue a temporary emergency gun violence restraining order orally based on the statements of a law enforcement officer made in accordance with subdivision (a) of Section 18140.\nSection 18145 (Penal Code): (2) If time and circumstances permit, a temporary emergency gun violence restraining order may be obtained in writing and based on a declaration signed under penalty of perjury."
